selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_turbine_cascade\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_turbine_cascade\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">plot_turbine_cascade</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">geometry</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">span_fraction</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.5</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">passages</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">3</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Every row at one span, unrolled flat: axial against pitchwise distance.</p><p>Suction sides are solid and pressure sides dashed. Each row shows\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">passages</span></code> neighbouring blades at its own pitch.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_turbine_spanwise\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_turbine_spanwise\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">plot_turbine_spanwise</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">geometry</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Each row\u2019s metal angles, measured gauging angle, throat and pitch, hub to tip.</p><p>The gauging angle <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">acos(throat/pitch)</span></code> is measured on the built blades;\nbeside the outlet metal angle it shows how far the section turns the flow\nfrom what it was drawn for. Line styles are the same in every row: see\nthe subplot titles.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_velocity_triangles\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_velocity_triangles\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">plot_velocity_triangles</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">turbine</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Each stage\u2019s rotor inlet and exit triangles, drawn from a common apex.</p><p>Velocities point down the page in the flow direction, with swirl across\nit, positive in the rotation direction. At each station the absolute\nvelocity <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c</span></code> is the relative velocity <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">w</span></code> plus the blade speed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">u</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_turbine_meridional\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.plot_turbine_meridional\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">plot_turbine_meridional</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">geometry</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The passage in (x, r), with rotating wall stretches, gaps and blade edges.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">geometry</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineGeometry</span></code>. Thick red\nstretches of wall turn with the shaft; the blade outlines are each row\u2019s\nleading and trailing edges and its tip or hub end.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#functions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.viz.turbine_viz\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Plotly figures of an axial turbine: triangles, passage, cascade and spanwise angles.</p><p>Each function takes one of the turbine objects and returns a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">go.Figure</span></code>,\nready for <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Report.add_figure()</span></code> or <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fig.show()</span></code>. Lengths are shown in\nmillimetres and angles in degrees. Pitchwise distances and angles are positive\nin the direction the rotor turns, as in <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../../turbine/index.html#module-pyskyfire.turbine\" title=\"pyskyfire.turbine\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.turbine</span></code></a>.</p>", "a[href=\"../../turbine/index.html#module-pyskyfire.turbine\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.turbine<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.turbine\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Axial turbine design: the duty, a meanline design, and the hardware it produces.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
